          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most homes, the answer is one large USB-C bank like the Anker 737 for the household, a small bank per person like the Anker Nano, and a crank weather radio like the Midland ER310 as the backstop. That covers phones, laptops, lights and information for a typical one-to-two-day outage for well under the cost of a power station, as long as you keep everything charged.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
